Patch-Source: FeralOS — fix for https://github.com/chimera-linux/sd-tools/issues/5
Subject: [PATCH] tmpfiles: give CONF_PATHS_STRV literal static storage duration

CONF_PATHS_STRV() expands to a C11 compound literal with automatic storage
duration scoped to the ENCLOSING BLOCK. In run() the literal is created inside
the switch() body and stored in config_dirs, then used AFTER the switch
(STRV_FOREACH debug loop, cat_config, read_config_files, parse_arguments).
That is a use-after-scope:

  case RUNTIME_SCOPE_SYSTEM:
          config_dirs = CONF_PATHS_STRV("tmpfiles.d");  /* literal dies here */
          break;
  }                                                        /* block ends */
  ...read_config_files(&c, config_dirs, ...)               /* dead stack */

clang happens to keep the (dead) stack slot intact, masking the bug; GCC 14+
actively reuses the slot (-Wdangling-pointer warns), so the strings turn into
garbage and sd-tmpfiles segfaults on every --create/--cat-config run
(stack-use-after-scope confirmed with ASan in upstream issue #5).

Fix: copy the four paths into an array with static storage duration so the
pointer stays valid for the lifetime of the program. CONF_PATHS_USR expands
to plain string-literal concatenations, so a file-scope array is valid.
--- a/src/tmpfiles/tmpfiles.c
+++ b/src/tmpfiles/tmpfiles.c
@@ -657,6 +657,18 @@
                  arg_dry_run ? (would) : (doing),       \
                  __VA_ARGS__)
 
+/* CONF_PATHS_STRV() compound literals have block-scoped automatic storage
+ * duration: storing the literal in config_dirs and using it after the
+ * switch reads dead stack memory — GCC 14+ reuses the slot and
+ * sd-tmpfiles segfaults on every --create (clang keeps the slot alive and
+ * only masks the bug). Keep the paths in static storage instead.
+ * Ref: https://github.com/chimera-linux/sd-tools/issues/5
+ */
+static const char *const system_config_dirs[] = {
+        CONF_PATHS_USR("tmpfiles.d"),
+        NULL,
+};
+
 static int user_config_paths(char*** ret) {
         _cleanup_strv_free_ char **config_dirs = NULL, **data_dirs = NULL;
         _cleanup_free_ char *persistent_config = NULL, *runtime_config = NULL, *data_home = NULL;
@@ -5549,7 +5561,7 @@
                 break;
 
         case RUNTIME_SCOPE_SYSTEM:
-                config_dirs = CONF_PATHS_STRV("tmpfiles.d");
+                config_dirs = (char **) system_config_dirs;
                 break;
 
         default:
